<title>SENEGAL: Senegal suspends fishing firms for illegal exports.</title>
<headline>Senegal suspends fishing firms for illegal exports.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal has suspended 10 fishing firms for dealing in illegal exports to Europe, a government official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Those companies were dealing with foreigners who have chosen to export fish illegally and don't want to make any investment here by paying taxes,&quot; Oceanography and Maritime Fishery department director Diagua Gueye told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;With such a procedure, fish goes out but the money from the fish is never back,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Senegal and the European Union signed a fishing agreement last March which included fishing rights for European vessels and extended the deal's coverage from two to four years.</p>
<p>--Abidjan newsroom, + 225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
